	(text "Programming / Debug -- ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 (U3) boot-strapping, buttons, native USB (J3)"
		(at 60 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7e1713ad-8183-40c7-a494-c1ee58fb375a")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels on this sheet yet. All resistors/caps/\nbuttons here are logically associated with U3 (ESP32-S3-WROOM-1, placed on\nconnectivity.kicad_sch) -- U3 itself is NOT re-instantiated on this sheet, per the\none-instance-per-part convention already used across this project's sheets.\nEspressif ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 Datasheet v1.8 (already cited in libs/components.csv),\nTable 4-1 'Default Configuration of Strapping Pins' + Section 4 'Boot Configurations':\n  R18 = GPIO0 (U3 pin 27) pull-up, 10k to +3V3_SYS -- GPIO0=1 selects SPI Boot\n        (normal boot); default is already weak-pull-up per Table 4-1, this makes\n        it explicit/robust rather than relying on the ~45k internal pull (Table 6-3).\n  R19 = GPIO3 (U3 pin 15) pull-down, 10k to GND -- Section 4.4 states this pin 'does\n        not have any internal pull resistors and the strapping value must be\n        controlled by an external circuit that cannot be in a high impedance state.'\n        Default eFuse JTAG-source config (Table 4-5) ignores GPIO3, so the pull\n        direction is not functionally critical yet, but a defined level is required.\n  R20 = GPIO45 (U3 pin 26) pull-down, 10k to GND -- selects VDD3P3_RTC-derived\n        3.3V SPI-flash voltage (Table 4-4), matching this module's 3.3V flash and\n        its own default weak-pull-down (Table 4-1).\n  R21 = GPIO46 (U3 pin 16) pull-down, 10k to GND -- required for a valid boot-mode\n        combination (GPIO46=1 with GPIO0=0 is explicitly invalid per Espressif);\n        matches its own default weak-pull-down (Table 4-1).\n  SW1 = BOOT button, GPIO0 to GND -- momentary override to enter Joint Download\n        Boot mode (GPIO0=0) for flashing.\n  R22 + C23 = EN (U3 pin 3) RC delay, 10k pull-up to +3V3_SYS + 1uF to GND -- per\n        the real Espressif ESP32-S3 Hardware Design Guidelines (Schematic Checklist,\n        docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-hardware-design-guidelines, ESP32-S3 section):\n        'The recommended setting for the RC delay circuit is usually R = 10 kOhm\n        and C = 1 uF.'\n  SW2 = RESET button, EN to GND -- momentary manual reset, standard practice."
		(at 60 38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "74d39709-11c7-4d65-96f8-134d18596681")
	)
	(text "Flashing/programming interface decision: NATIVE USB via ESP32-S3's built-in\nUSB-OTG peripheral (U3 pins 13/14, USB_D-/USB_D+ per connectivity.kicad_sch),\nnot a separate UART-to-USB bridge IC. Reasoning: ESP32-S3 has a full-speed USB 2.0\nOTG peripheral plus a USB-Serial/JTAG controller with CDC-ACM emulation built in\n(ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 Datasheet v1.8, Sections 5.2.1.7/5.2.1.8) -- 'Internal PHY, so no\nor very few external components needed to connect to a host computer' and 'CDC-ACM\nsupports host controllable chip reset and entry into download mode', and Table 4-3\n'Joint Download Boot' explicitly lists 'USB-Serial-JTAG Download Boot'/'USB-OTG\nDownload Boot' as supported methods -- so no extra bridge IC (e.g. CH340/CP2102)\nis needed, saving part count/cost/board area on a board that already has USB-C\nconnectors for power. HOWEVER: the existing USB-C receptacle on power_bms.kicad_sch\n(J2, Connector:USB_C_Receptacle_PowerOnly_6P) is POWER-ONLY -- it has no D+/D-\npins at all, so it cannot carry the native-USB data lines. Since power_bms.kicad_sch\nis out of scope for this task (must not be touched), this sheet places a SECOND,\ndedicated data-capable USB-C receptacle (J3, Connector:USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0_14P,\na real KiCad-default part with D+/D- pins) purely for programming/debug. R23/R24\nare J3's CC1/CC2 5.1k pulldowns (to GND), matching the same UFP-device convention\nalready used for J2 on power_bms.kicad_sch (5.1k per USB-C spec so any host/PD\nadapter enables VBUS at default 5V/current). A future hardware revision could\ninstead swap J2 for a combined power+data USB-C receptacle to avoid a second\nconnector -- flagged as an open concern in regulation_notes.md/README, not fixed\nhere since power_bms.kicad_sch cannot be edited in this pass."
		(at 60 100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a18f2802-5674-4b2b-b55a-c57d401b77ae")
	)
